{
	// DRAFT: Unused, shows how it can look like.
	"$module": "voxen::gfx::LandStructs",
	"$schema": "gfx-structs",

	PseudoSurfaceVertexPosition: {
		comment: 'Pseudo-chunk surface vertex positions are stored in a separate stream',
		fields: [
			{ name: 'pos_exchunkspace_unorm', type: 'uint16_t3', comment:
'Vertex position in "extended" chunk-local space to allow\n\
going slightly out of chunk bounds for stitching/skirting.\n\
After UNORM unpacking expand it into [-0.125:1.125] range.'
			},
		],
	},

	PseudoSurfaceVertexAttributes: {
		comment: 'Pseudo-chunk surface vertex attributes except positions',
		fields: [
			{ name: 'normal_octpack_snorm', type: 'int16_t2', comment:
'Normal compressed using octahedral method, then packed into two 16-bit SNORM values.\n\
Octahedral method is taken from paper "A Survey of Efficient Representations for Independent Unit Vectors":\n\
http://jcgt.org/published/0003/02/01/paper.pdf\n\
The only difference is that Y and Z axes are swapped in this implementation.'
			},
			{ name: 'mat_hist_entries', type: 'uint16_t4', comment:
'Material histogram (MatHist) stores up to 4 materials with the "highest presence"\n\
in this vertex. This attribute is guaranteed to be the same for all three vertices\n\
comprising a triangle.\n\
An entry is a 16-bit value which can be treated as either material ID if its highest\n\
bit is zero ([0:2^15) range) or as fixed R5G5B5 color otherwise ([2^15:2^16) range).\n\
Material ID assignment and encoding/decoding of colors is the responsibility\n\
of block registry system, and is not covered here.'
			},
			{ name: 'mat_hist_weights', type: 'uint8_t4', comment:
'Blending weights of `mat_hist_entries` elements, full range [0; 255].\n\
Zero weight means the entry is ignored, it can then contain garbage data.\n\n\
While the exact blending process is up to the renderer, these values are\n\
calculated relative to each other - basically they define a weighted sum.'
			},
		]
	},

	PseudoSurfaceDrawCommand: {
		fields: [
			{ name: 'pos_data_address', type: 'gpuaddr' },
			{ name: 'attrib_data_address', type: 'gpuaddr' },
			{ name: 'chunk_base_camworld', type: 'float3' },
			{ name: 'chunk_size_metres', type: 'float' },
		]
	},
}
